    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows consolidation around 85-90 EUR; true outcomes frequently drop 10-20% below the forecast before recovering.",
    "Forecast fails to account for mean reversion after a spike in sentiment (e.g., 0.20); model assumes linear growth while price often reverses sharply within 3-5 days.",
    "Model overestimates volatility recovery; it predicts smooth upward trends where true outcomes show high-frequency oscillation between 78 and 95 EUR.",
    "When sentiment history is flat (0.00) or low, the model's linear extrapolation leads to significant overshoots of 10-15 EUR compared to actual price action.",
    "Forecast horizon error: Model assumes monotonic increase over 30 days, whereas true outcomes display a 'V' shape with an initial crash followed by a delayed recovery."
